From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:56:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] manifest: raise the FCM target level to 7, the oldest 24.0
 ships

check_vintf cannot find a framework matrix for the level this declared:

  ERROR: No such file or directory: Cannot find framework matrix at FCM
  version 5.

24.0 ships compatibility_matrix.7.xml and .8.xml plus the dated ones, so 5
has nothing to compare against and 7 is the most permissive level available.
Raising it asserts compliance with a newer matrix than this hardware was
designed against; check_vintf reports any HAL that assertion gets wrong, so
the claim is checked rather than assumed.

---
 manifest.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/manifest.xml b/manifest.xml
index 4ffb8f6a..39eb1d4e 100644
--- a/manifest.xml
+++ b/manifest.xml
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-<manifest version="1.0" type="device" target-level="5">
+<manifest version="1.0" type="device" target-level="7">
     <hal format="hidl">
         <name>android.hardware.audio</name>
         <transport>hwbinder</transport>
